A||N||3||David Bartlett||E-Brake Cables - Longest Lasting?||||1||
Z||000000||David Bartlett||11-25-2001||11:05 AM||||Do we have a choice when it comes to E-Brake Cables? Can you buy ones with Stainless steel protection so they don't seize?<BR>Let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-25-2001||03:59 PM||||None I'm aware of.<P>When I lived in NY I used to coat the jacket every so often with brake grease. It doesn't wash off like oil based and you don't risk hardening or swelling the nylon used inside many of these cables. You just need a very thin film on them. A little brake grease under the boot on the caliper end will also help seal out water etc. If the cable has a plastic tube over the metal jacket, work a little brake grease under the ends to seal it. <P>The brake grease will be worked into the small cracks in the metal jacket durring application. It will tend to stay there unless hit with a pressure washer or something. Even if you get some exterior rust the cable will have a much harder time wicking water inside. <P>Dielectric grease will also work for this. May even work better. That stuff has a silicone oil in it that will wick into the jacket and be very hard to wash out.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||11-25-2001||07:53 PM||||I've used a couple different brands of aftermarket cables before I realized that I could get GM originals for about half the price. I don't know which last the longest, but the GM ones are much better quality. Some of the aftermarket ones were very poorly made.<P>GM part #<BR>10200441<BR>10200442<BR>$11.85 each from <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsdirect.com</A> <BR>$10.85 each from <A HREF="http://www.auto-parts-for-less.com/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.auto-parts-for-less.com/index.html</A> <BR>or check your local dealer.||||reg||7
Z||000003||artherd||11-26-2001||03:19 AM||||Got GM part numbers for the *88* cables? (are they different?)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
